1
00:00:00,070 --> 00:00:02,390
Try snapping spaghetti into two pieces.

2
00:00:03,250 --> 00:00:03,950
You can't.

3
00:00:04,280 --> 00:00:06,780
It breaks into three or more, almost every

4
00:00:06,780 --> 00:00:09,220
time. Even Richard Feynman couldn't

5
00:00:09,220 --> 00:00:10,050
explain why.

6
00:00:10,410 --> 00:00:12,230
When the stick snaps in the middle, each

7
00:00:12,230 --> 00:00:13,760
half springs back.

8
00:00:14,060 --> 00:00:15,720
That sends a bending wave down the

9
00:00:15,720 --> 00:00:17,900
pieces... and they snap again.

10
00:00:18,200 --> 00:00:20,940
In 2018, a team at MIT found the

11
00:00:20,940 --> 00:00:24,200
trick: twist it almost a full turn first,

12
00:00:24,540 --> 00:00:25,240
then bend.

13
00:00:25,530 --> 00:00:28,090
The twist soaks up the wave, and it

14
00:00:28,090 --> 00:00:29,170
breaks cleanly in two.

15
00:00:30,110 --> 00:00:30,790
Now try it.
